{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>And they shall not bear iniquity.</b> Rashi explained: from here we learned that one who serves lacking garments is liable to death. And Rabbi Yitzchak son of Rabbi Avraham, of blessed memory, raised a difficulty: for in the chapter אלו הן הנחנקין he derives it from a verse in the section nearby: ״והיתה להם כהונה לחקת עולם״, and we expound: when their garments are upon them, their priesthood is upon them; when their garments are not upon them, their priesthood is not upon them — and they are considered zarim, and a zar who serves is liable to death, as it is said: ״וזר הקרב יומת״. And one may answer that this verse is needed for the sake of the michnasayim, which is not explicit in the verse that follows."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:14.414346855Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}